            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            etc.) as well as on higher/homotopical versions like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} L-infinity algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"} A-infinity algebra
            etc.
          %p
            There are also few pages on various invariants of algebraic objects or operations on algebraic expressions, e.g. on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resultants"} resultants
            of polynomials,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            of a matrix,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasideterminant"} quasideterminant
            of a matrix with noncommutative entries.
          %p
            For many algebraic structures a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            is defined; they embody “symmetry algebras” of some other algebraic objects. An action is expressed via a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of one object as a subobject of a full object of another; or as a combination of the object which acts and which is acted upon (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            of the appropriate kind (possibly dualized:
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodule"} comodule
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contramodule"} contramodule
            = succeed ";" do
